	"source": "Generations 1-3: the item tables of the pret disassemblies (pokered data/items/prices.asm, pokecrystal data/items/attributes.asm, pokeemerald src/data/items.h, pokefirered src/data/items.json). Generation 4 goods sold outside the Poké Mart (herbs, evolution stones, drinks, Poké Doll, Dive Ball): pokeplatinum res/items/data and pokeheartgold files/itemtool/itemdata/item_data.csv. Later games: researched from Bulbapedia and Serebii shop tables (see note).",
	"note": "Buy prices of the everyday goods PokéTale sells (story/shop.mjs), by the game whose disc standard a region has (story/machine-standards.mjs). Crystal stands for Gold/Silver, Emerald for Ruby/Sapphire. Goods sold outside the Poké Mart take the regular price of a regular seller (herb shop, stone shop, vending machine; one-off markets such as Black City are left out), else the price the game lists for them. tools/build-shop.mjs keeps the ones that differ from today's price in data/shop.json.",
